========================================================================
  FASTER FORMULAS FOR TOURNAMENT SEQUENCES
  opus-2026-03-22-S166
========================================================================

FORMULA 1: E[H] = n!/2^{n-1} — EXACT, O(1)
------------------------------------------------------------

  n= 2: E[H] = 1 = 1.0000
  n= 3: E[H] = 3/2 = 1.5000
  n= 4: E[H] = 3 = 3.0000
  n= 5: E[H] = 15/2 = 7.5000
  n= 6: E[H] = 45/2 = 22.5000
  n= 7: E[H] = 315/4 = 78.7500
  n= 8: E[H] = 315 = 315.0000
  n= 9: E[H] = 2835/2 = 1417.5000
  n=10: E[H] = 14175/2 = 7087.5000
  n=11: E[H] = 155925/4 = 38981.2500

  This is EXACT and needs no enumeration.
  PROOF: each permutation σ is a Hamiltonian path of T
  with probability 1/2^{n-1} (each of n-1 consecutive arcs
  must go the right way). E[H] = n!/2^{n-1} by linearity.


FORMULA 2: E[H²] — THE SECOND MOMENT
------------------------------------------------------------

  E[H²] = Σ_{σ,τ} P(both σ,τ are HP)
        = (1/2^{2(n-1)}) × Σ_{σ,τ} 2^{overlap(σ,τ)}

  n=2: E[H²] = 1 = 1.0000, Var(H) = 0 = 0.0000
  n=3: E[H²] = 3 = 3.0000, Var(H) = 3/4 = 0.7500
  n=4: E[H²] = 12 = 12.0000, Var(H) = 3 = 3.0000
  n=5: E[H²] = 1185/16 = 74.0625, Var(H) = 285/16 = 17.8125
  n=6: E[H²] = 1305/2 = 652.5000, Var(H) = 585/4 = 146.2500

  W(n) = F_n(2)/n! = E[H²]/(E[H])² × (n!/2^{n-1})²:
    n=1: W = 1
    n=2: W = 2
    n=3: W = 8
    n=4: W = 32
    n=5: W = 158
    n=6: W = 928
    n=7: W = 6350
    n=8: W = 49752


FORMULA 3: Var(H) FROM W(n)
------------------------------------------------------------

  If we know W(n), we can compute Var(H) without enumeration:
    E[H] = n!/2^{n-1}
    E[H²] = W(n) × (E[H])² / n! × 2^{2(n-1)} / 2^{C(n,2)}

  Actually: W(n) = E[H²] × n! / (E[H])²
  So: E[H²] = W(n) × (E[H])² / n!
  And: Var(H) = E[H²] - (E[H])²

  n=1: W=1, E[H]=1, Var(H) = 0 = 0.0000, match=True
  n=2: W=2, E[H]=1, Var(H) = 0 = 0.0000, match=True
  n=3: W=8, E[H]=3/2, Var(H) = 3/4 = 0.7500, match=True
  n=4: W=32, E[H]=3, Var(H) = 3 = 3.0000, match=True
  n=5: W=158, E[H]=15/2, Var(H) = 285/16 = 17.8125, match=True
  n=6: W=928, E[H]=45/2, Var(H) = 585/4 = 146.2500, match=True


